# Auto-deploy refluxtweaks.com

When the user asks you to build, change, fix, or improve anything on the **refluxtweaks.com website** (this repo):

1. Complete the requested website work.
2. Run `npm run build` when you changed app code, styles, or components (skip only for pure copy or config-only edits if build is unnecessary).
3. **Automatically commit and push to `main`** — do not wait for the user to ask separately.
4. Use a clear commit message focused on why the change helps users.
5. Tell the user the commit hash and that it is pushed live.

## Exceptions — do NOT auto-push without explicit approval

- Changes that include secrets (`.env`, credentials, API keys)
- `private/downloads/REFLUX-PRO-Setup.exe` or other large binaries unless the user asked to update installers
- The user explicitly says "don't push", "local only", or "don't commit"

## Push workflow

```bash
git status
git diff --stat
git add <relevant files>
git commit -m "..."
git push origin main
```

If push to `main` is blocked, retry with approval rather than leaving changes uncommitted.
